window.TERMS=(window.TERMS||[]).concat(["Albedo|The fraction of sunlight that a surface reflects.","Barangay|The smallest administrative division in the Philippines.","Baybayin|A pre-colonial writing system of the Philippines.","Bilateral contract|A direct agreement to buy and sell power outside the spot market.","Big Bang|The rapid expansion from which the universe began about 13.8 billion years ago.","Biosphere|The part of Earth where life exists.","Black start|Restarting a power station without outside electricity.","Bronze Age|The period when bronze was the main metal for tools, roughly 3300 to 1200 BCE.","Busbar|A metal bar that carries heavy current inside a substation.","Capacity|The maximum output a power plant can produce.","Cenozoic|The era since 66 million years ago, often called the age of mammals.","Circuit breaker|A switch that automatically cuts power when a fault occurs.","Cordillera|A system of parallel mountain ranges.","Dark matter|Invisible matter detected only through its gravity.","Distribution|The final stage of delivering electricity to customers at lower voltage.","Encomienda|A Spanish colonial system granting settlers the labor and tribute of local people.","Exoplanet|A planet that orbits a star other than the Sun.","Feeder|A line that carries power from a substation to customers.","Forced outage|An unplanned loss of a generating unit or transmission line.","Futures|Contracts to buy or sell at a set price on a future date.","Galleon|A large sailing ship used by Spain for transpacific trade.","Grounding|Connecting equipment to the earth for safety.","Harmonics|Distortions in an alternating-current waveform.","Heat rate|The fuel energy a plant needs to produce one unit of electricity.","Hedge|A trade made to reduce the risk of price changes.","Homo sapiens|The species of modern humans.","Intramuros|The walled historic core of Manila.","Iron Age|The period when iron became the main metal for tools.","Light-year|The distance light travels in a year, about 9.46 trillion km.","Load shedding|Deliberately cutting power to some customers to protect the grid.","Mangrove|A salt-tolerant tree that grows along tropical coasts.","Marginal cost|The cost of producing one more unit.","Mesozoic|The era of the dinosaurs, from about 252 to 66 million years ago.","Neolithic|The late Stone Age, marked by farming and settled villages.","Outage|A period when a power plant or line is out of service.","Overload|Current beyond what equipment is designed to carry.","PAGASA|The Philippine national weather agency.","Paleolithic|The early Stone Age, before farming.","Paleozoic|The era from about 539 to 252 million years ago.","Parsec|A unit of distance equal to about 3.26 light-years.","Phase|One of the alternating currents in a three-phase power system.","Power factor|The ratio of useful power to total power in an AC circuit.","Price cap|A maximum allowed price.","Redshift|The stretching of light from receding objects toward the red end of the spectrum.","Relay|A device that switches a circuit in response to a signal.","Ring of Fire|The belt of volcanoes and earthquake zones around the Pacific Ocean.","Settlement|The financial process of paying for traded electricity.","Solar wind|A stream of charged particles flowing from the Sun.","Spinning reserve|Generating capacity already online and ready to raise output quickly.","Sunspot|A cooler, darker patch on the Sun’s surface.","Switchgear|Equipment used to control, protect and isolate electrical equipment.","Synchronous|Running in step with the grid frequency.","Tagalog|A language of central Luzon that is the basis of Filipino.","Topography|The shape and features of land surfaces.","Transmission line|A high-voltage line that carries electricity over long distances.","Volatility|How sharply a price moves up and down.","Watt-hour|The energy used by one watt over one hour.","Zenith|The point in the sky directly overhead."]);

