window.TERMS=(window.TERMS||[]).concat(["Aftershock|A smaller earthquake that follows a larger one.","Allele|One version of a gene.","Ambassador|A diplomat who represents a country abroad.","Amendment|A change to a constitution or law.","Arbitrage|Profiting from price differences between markets.","Baroque|An ornate European art style of the 17th and early 18th centuries.","Bay|A curved inlet of the sea.","Bear market|A period of falling prices.","Biofuel|Fuel made from plants or waste.","Biomass|The total mass of living things, or plant material used as fuel.","Bond|A loan to a government or company that pays interest.","Bull market|A period of rising prices.","Caldera|A large crater formed when a volcano collapses.","Calligraphy|The art of beautiful handwriting.","Cape|A point of land extending into the sea.","Cloud computing|Using remote servers over the internet instead of local ones.","Dividend|A payment of profit to shareholders.","El Niño|A warming of the central Pacific that alters weather around the world.","Encryption|Scrambling data so that only authorized people can read it.","Epicenter|The point on the surface directly above an earthquake’s origin.","Epic|A long poem that tells of heroic deeds.","Equity|Ownership in a company.","Ethanol|An alcohol used as a fuel and in drinks.","Federalism|A system that divides power between central and regional governments.","Firewall|Software or hardware that blocks unauthorized network traffic.","Folklore|The traditional stories and customs of a people.","Fresco|A painting made on wet plaster.","Genotype|An organism’s genetic makeup.","Gulf|A large inlet of the sea.","Island arc|A chain of volcanic islands above a subduction zone.","Karst|A landscape of caves and sinkholes formed by dissolving limestone.","La Niña|A cooling of the central Pacific that alters weather around the world.","Lagoon|A shallow body of water separated from the sea by a reef or sand bar.","Lahar|A volcanic mudflow.","Liquidity|How easily an asset can be turned into cash.","Magnitude|A measure of an earthquake’s size.","Mitochondria|The parts of a cell that release energy.","Monopoly|A market with a single seller.","Mutation|A change in DNA.","Mythology|A collection of traditional stories about gods and heroes.","Nanometer|One billionth of a meter.","Natural selection|The process by which helpful traits become more common.","Oligopoly|A market dominated by a few sellers.","Osmosis|The movement of water across a membrane.","Phenotype|An organism’s observable traits.","Photovoltaic|Converting sunlight directly into electricity.","Pilgrimage|A journey to a sacred place.","Plebiscite|A direct vote by the people on an issue.","Pyroclastic flow|A fast-moving cloud of hot gas and ash from a volcano.","Recession|A significant fall in economic activity lasting months.","Referendum|A vote on a single proposal.","Reef|A ridge of rock or coral near the sea surface.","Rift|A crack where Earth’s crust is pulling apart.","Semiconductor|A material whose conductivity can be controlled.","Shield volcano|A broad volcano with gentle slopes.","Sinkhole|A hole formed when the ground collapses.","Speciation|The formation of new species.","Stalactite|A mineral formation hanging from a cave ceiling.","Stock|A share of ownership in a company.","Storm surge|A rise in sea level driven by a storm.","Stratovolcano|A steep volcano built of layers of lava and ash.","Subduction|The sinking of one tectonic plate beneath another.","Suffrage|The right to vote.","Supply|The quantity of a good that sellers offer.","Taxonomy|The science of classifying organisms.","Trade deficit|A situation in which a country imports more than it exports.","Trench|A deep, narrow valley in the ocean floor.","Veto|The power to reject a decision or law."]);

